"[2511.01850v1] SmartMLOps Studio: Design of an LLM-Integrated IDE with Automated MLOps Pipelines for Model Development and Monitoring (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.01850v1)\nciteturn2257view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.01850v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.02770v1] Beyond Single Embeddings: Capturing Diverse Targets with Multi-Query Retrieval (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.02770v1)\nciteturn2257view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.02770v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 160\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.02776v1] XR-1: Towards Versatile Vision-Language-Action Models via Learning Unified Vision-Motion Representations (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.02776v1)\nciteturn2257view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.02776v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.02919v1] Cache Mechanism for Agent RAG Systems (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.02919v1)\nciteturn2257view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn2242view0\",\"lineno\":8}); Total lines: 159\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 4 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:Cache Mechanism for Agent RAG Systems\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Shuhang Lin , cite6†Zhencan Peng , cite7†Lingyao Li , cite8†Xiao Lin , cite9†Xi Zhu , cite10†Yongfeng Zhang L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Cache Mechanism for Agent RAG Systems, by Shuhang Lin and 5 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite11†View PDF cite12†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Recent advances in Large Language Model (LLM)-based agents have been propelled by Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), which grants the models access to vast external knowledge bases. Despite RAG's success in improving agent performance, agent-level cache management, particularly constructing, maintaining, and updating a compact, relevant corpus dynamically tailored to each agent's need, remains underexplored.\nL17: Therefore, we introduce ARC (Agent RAG Cache Mechanism), a novel, annotation-free caching framework that dynamically manages small, high-value corpora for each agent. By synthesizing historical query distribution patterns with the intrinsic geometry of cached items in the embedding space, ARC automatically maintains a high-relevance cache.\nL18: With comprehensive experiments on three retrieval datasets, our experimental results demonstrate that ARC reduces storage requirements to 0.015% of the original corpus while offering up to 79.8% has-answer rate and reducing average retrieval latency by 80%. Our results demonstrate that ARC can drastically enhance efficiency and effectiveness in RAG-powered LLM agents.\nL19: Subjects:  | Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite13†arXiv:2511.02919 [cs.CL]\nL21:    | (or cite14†arXiv:2511.02919v1 [cs.CL] for this version)\nL22:    | cite15†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.02919†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Shuhang Lin [cite16†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Tue, 4 Nov 2025 19:02:29 UTC (535 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Cache Mechanism for Agent RAG Systems, by Shuhang Lin and 5 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite11†View PDF L35: